# Arithva does not need any API key to run.
#
# Speech recognition and speech synthesis use the browser's Web Speech API, and
# intent routing is rule-based, so the demo works offline apart from the weather
# call. This is deliberate: a live demo should not be able to fail because a
# model endpoint is slow or a key expired.
#
# The optional settings below are for later work.

# Where the frontend should reach the API. Empty means same origin.
# ARITHVA_API_BASE=

# Optional: ElevenLabs for the spoken replies.
#
# Without this, Arithva speaks with the browser's built-in voice and everything
# still works. With it, replies use ElevenLabs, and if any call fails (bad key,
# quota reached, slow network) it falls back to the browser voice automatically.
#
# Copy this file to .env and paste your key there. NEVER commit .env.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
#
# Both optional. Defaults are in backend/tools/speech_tool.py.
# VERIFY the voice and model in your ElevenLabs dashboard, and listen to a
# sample in each language you plan to demo before relying on them.
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=
# ELEVENLABS_MODEL_ID=eleven_multilingual_v2

# Optional: a hosted speech model for better Kannada recognition than the
# browser's. Not wired up yet.
# BHASHINI_API_KEY=
# BHASHINI_USER_ID=

# Optional: an LLM for intent routing on sentences the keyword router misses.
# The model would still never produce a number; tools do that.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
